  "conv": {
    "about": "A conversation's own facts (Docs/Design/84 §7.11), read as conv.X: the move just made and the one before it (moves.json's names), the tone of the line before, and the lines said so far. Any other conv.X is a tag a line set ({X=value}). Phase 4: interrupt, what broke the talk off (§8.10; the next line is a break line), and stake, why a third joined (§8.9; Phase 5 adds favourite: the talk is on their favourite topic). Phase 5: topic, the topic the talk is on now (it may turn: a pivot), goal, the goal a line is a step of (frames.json's goals, §8.5), and aspect, the tier of the topic they are at (topics.json's aspects: a pair that has talked of it before starts one deeper). Phase 6 (§8.8): issue, the issue an opinion was given on (opinions.json's), issue_words, how it is spoken of (\"the Watch\"), agree, whether the one speaking and the one spoken to stand on the same side of it (half: one of them is mixed), agreed_before, how it went the last time the two aired it (pair.agree.<issue>); stake gains stance (a third who holds the issue strongly). Phase 8 (§8.5): from, the topic a talk turns from, while a pivot's own line is chosen (a line made for that step).",
